AB  - Deep Reinforcement Learning is a highly emerging Framework in the context of mathematical decision making in optimization applications, probability theory and artificial intelligence. RN is a type of machine learning wherein there is no supervision and the agent must figure out what action to take and in which space. In RL, there is a mathematical basis of learning the best policies after interacting with some environment, premised by trial-and-error and mathematical models that capture the behavior of the environment-Decision processes with Markov features, Bellman equations, dynamic programming, stochastic control, and so on. Fundamentally, RL is a decision-making formalism in the form of a sequential optimization problem, in which an agent is informed of what action to perform in observed states by maximising the total received rewards. At this point we would like to override the Pure Theory of RL such as value functions, or policy evaluation, or explorationexploitation tradeoff etc, by considering learning as a learning process, which can be iterated around the reward signal that the agent receives in response to some action in some state. Conventional RL techniques, including Q-learning, SARSA and policy gradient techniques generate an effective approximation of the optimal policy based on algebraic equations. Healthcare has also applied RL algorithms to assist in planning treatments and customizing medicine by recommending the optimal treatment to provide to each patient based on their response. These applications point out the fact that RL is able to characterize decision processes that are uncertain, delayed payoffs, and long-term strategy. Editorial Note RL is also developing to solve combinatorial optimization problems, where a decision is to choose the optimal combination of variables, with constraints. The use of RL has been applied in traffic control system optimization, supply chain logistics and managing the energy grid whereby solutions are able to gradually evolve in their optimal decision-making based on historical information and real-time situations.
